Elif leads me to the large espresso machine.
It gleams and is a donation for the café.
I have never used a machine like this before.
"You need a little patience," Elif explains.
I watch her closely.
First she grinds the coffee.
Then she presses the powder down really firmly.
After that, a perfect espresso runs into the cup.
It smells fantastic in the room.
I really have to learn to operate the machine properly.
"Now it is your turn," says Elif.
The café is still empty and very quiet.
We have time and practice together with the coffee grounds.
"Not too firm and not too loose," Elif helps me.
Unfortunately, my first attempt is wrong.
Some powder falls on the table.
I try it a second time right away.
This time it already feels much better.
